AB  - Study Objective: We describe the course of a patient who underwent staged, fertility-sparing treatment of Placenta Accreta Spectrum (PAS) diagnosed at 13 weeks gestation in the setting of missed abortion. She ultimately underwent dilation and evacuation with hysteroscopic placental resection, interval uterine artery embolization, and subsequent robotic isthmocele repair. Design: Surgical video Setting: Large academic community hospital and surgery center. Patients or Participants: This case report details the course of a single patient undergoing fertility-sparing management of PAS in the setting of a 13-week fetal demise. She gave verbal and written consent for her de-identified patient information to be used to complete this video-based case report, including consent for surgical videos and imaging to be used. Interventions: The patient underwent directly visualized uterine evacuation including partial hysteroscopic resection of morbidly adherent placental tissue with electrocauterization of remaining bleeding tissue. Three weeks later, she experienced delayed bleeding and underwent Uterine Artery Embolization (UAE) with Vascular Interventional Radiology (VIR) with good effect. Two weeks after UAE, she underwent a Magnetic Resonance Imaging study which demonstrated possible retained placental tissue and also revealed a uterine isthmocele in the lower uterine segment. Forty-eight days after the initial hysteroscopic resection, she underwent uncomplicated, hysteroscopically-guided, robotically-assisted laparoscopic isthmocele repair. Measurements and Primary Results: This patient underwent successful uterine-sparing treatment for PAS disorder including UAE for delayed post-procedural bleeding following hysteroscopic placental resection. At the time of isthmocele repair, pathology of intrauterine contents showed no remaining products of conception. Following isthmocele repair, she had an uncomplicated post-operative course. Conclusion: This case report discusses a 27-year-old G4P3013 undergoing staged, fertility-sparing treatment of PAS with hysteroscopic placental resection, UAE and hysteroscopically-guided isthmocele repair.
DO  - 10.1016/j.jmig.2025.09.370
