AB  - Study Objective: The Objective of this Video presentation is to demonstrate various presentations and techniques in the management of Uterine Isthmoceles. Design: This submission details three case presentations of uterine isthmocele, their pre-operative evaluation, counseling, and operative technique for treatment. Setting: All patients were placed in lithotomy position. Two patients had robotic surgery with concurrent Hysteroscopy. One patient had only a hysteroscopy with plan for interval laparoscopic repair. Patients or Participants: This case series represents three patients with uterine isthmocele Interventions: Each patient underwent either surgical management alone or a combination of medical and surgical management depending on the specific details of their cases. Measurements and Main Results: Each patient underwent surgical repair and are currently awaiting follow-up. In the case of the two patients treated for pregnancy, their beta-hcg values trended down to zero following repair. In the case of the non-pregnant patient, her isthmocele was repaired and interval saline-infusion sonogram demonstrated an improved residual myometrial thickness of 7.6mm from 1.8mm. Conclusion: Uterine isthmocele present challenges in the care of OBGYN patient both during pregnancy and outside of pregnancy. A multidisciplanary approach to care often times involving medical and surgical therapies, can be necessary for proper treatment of patients with isthmocele- related complications.
DO  - 10.1016/j.jmig.2024.09.185
