AB  - Cesarean scar pregnancy (CSP) is one of the rarest forms of ectopic pregnancy with devastating complications. It occurs due to the implantation of gestational sac into the myometrial defect of previous cesarean scar, the niche. We are presenting a series of three case reports of CSP who were diagnosed and treated in Alorf hospital over a two-year duration. Painless vaginal bleeding during the first trimester was the most common symptom. Methods of diagnosis and mode of treatment were described and discussed in relation to various medical literatures.
