AB  - Case of para 1 after A stage 1 CS in previous pregnancy came with post-menstrual spotting of dark brown blood and intermenstrual spotting. She had TVS and HSG showing a uterine niche at the site of CS scar. After which, she had a MRI to delineate the defect before planning of surgery for repair. After careful counselling and explaining that the repair is aimed at symptomatic relief rather than improving the fertility, she agreed for hysteroscopy and laparoscopic repair. The video shows the repair being carried out. Hysteroscopy was performed first to delineate the defect, and then, laparoscopic resection of the repair was done. The area of the defect was transilluminated to show the defect. The vescicovaginal fold was opened and bladder reflected down. After this, the defect was resected and repaired with interrupted PDS sutures. The area was again hysteroscopically transluminated, but the defect was not apparent. This is an interesting and educational video demonstration of an uncommon surgical procedure. She has had a spontaneous conception since then and is currently 8-week pregnant.
DO  - 10.1111/1471-0528.7-15703
