AB  - Objective: To demonstrate our experience with hysteroscopic treatment of cesarean scar defect (CSD). Design: Surgical video article. Settings: University hospital. Patients: Patient A: A 42-year-old patient with one previous cesarean delivery. She complained of two weeks of postmenstrual spotting. MRI shows a 4.5x13x6.2mm-CSD, with a residual myometrial thickness of 3.1 mm. Patient B (with poly-like structure): A 36-year-old patient with two previous cesarean deliveries. She complained of ten days of postmenstrual spotting. MRI shows a 9.2x13.6x6mm-CSD, with a residual myometrial of 2.6 mm. Patient C (with cyst-like formation): A 42-year-old patient with three previous cesarean deliveries. She complained of two weeks of postmenstrual spotting with frequent urge to urinate for six years. MRI shows a 7x7x13mm-CSD, with a residual myometrial thickness of 3.5 mm. Patient D (with cyst-like formation): A 36-year-old patient with two previous cesarean deliveries. She complained of one week of postmenstrual spotting. MRI shows a 9.2x13.6x6mm-CSD, with a residual myometrial thickness 2.6 mm. Patient E (with ectopic endometrium): A 36-year-old patient with one previous cesarean delivery. She complained of one week of postmenstrual spotting and infertility for two years. MRI shows a 13x13.8x3.4mm-CSD, with a residual myometrial thickness of 2.5 mm. Patient F (with perforation): A 34-year-old patient with one previous cesarean delivery. She complained of ten days of postmenstrual spotting. MRI shows a 17x10x15mm-CSD, with a residual myometrial thickness of 3.5 mm. Interventions: The hysteroscope was introduced under direct visualization, and after determining the location of the defect, a cutting loop was used to remove the fibrotic tissue flap under the pouchlike defect, from the bottom of the defect to the endocervical canal. And the niche surface will be superficially coagulated. Polyps and cysts in the niche were resected. Abnormal vascular patterns and endometrium were coagulated thoroughly. Measurements/Results: All these patients' postmenstrual spotting stopped after the surgery. Conclusions: Hysteroscopic niche treatment reduced postmenstrual spotting and spotting-related discomfort.
DO  - 10.1016/j.jmig.2018.09.243
