AB  - Cesarean scar defect or isthmocele is a relatively newly recognised entity. Patients with previous cesarean section can have this complication. There is no consensus on the definition or management, but it is usually identified as a triangular defect at the area of prior hysterotomy on pelvic imaging. This pathology can cause abnormal uterine bleeding and chronic pelvic pain among other symptoms. Laparoscopic and hysteroscopic treatment have been described in small case reports and series.We present a case of laparoscopic repair of a cesarean scar defect. Step by step technique is demonstrated.
DO  - 10.1016/j.jmig.2017.08.454
