AB  - Combined Hysteroscopic and Laparoscopic Repair of Isthmocele presents a rare case of isthmocele diagnosed after cesarean section scar ectopic pregnancy treated successfully with methotrexate and uterine artery embolisation. Patient was advised against future pregnancies. After MRI and SIS confirmation, video demonstrates combined hysteroscopic approach-transillumination and laparoscopic excision and repair of the isthmocele. We also emphasize the importance of different techniques for decreasing blood loss-tourniquet and vasopressin administration. Defect was repaired with multilayer closure, including final imbricating baseball stitch technique.Following the repair, hysteroscopy was repeated demonstrating resolution of the defect.
DO  - 10.1016/j.jmig.2017.08.311
