AB  - The aim of this video abstract is demonstrate the technical aprroach of bladder dissection in three different cases which has been classified basic to difficult. First patient has no previous surgery so that we presented basic approach. In second case, who has a previous cesarean sections, the seroza of the bladder is adherent to anterior wall of the uterus and and dissection was performed with lateral approach. Last case demonstrates us that unusual placement of bladder in the defect of cesarean scar, and adhesions were incised with laparoscopic cold scissors. The ceramic cup of clermont-ferrrand uterin manipulator and breisky vaginal valve was used to pointing out the anterior vaginal fornix in our technique. Early and late complications were not detected. Urinary catheter was kept one week in the last case. Spontan urination was observed in all patients after surgery.
