AB  - An isthmocele is a pouch-like defect in the anterior uterine wall at the site of a cesarean section scar. Common symptoms include abnormal uterine bleeding, pelvic pain and secondary infertility. The abnormal bleeding is often described as bleeding that persists for days or weeks after ones menses has ended. It is often diagnosed with ultrasound, sonohysterogram, and hysteroscopy. Our patient presented with post-menstrual bleeding and pelvic pain after her second cesarean section and was found to have an isthmocele on sonohysterogram. In this video we present a technique of a hysteroscopy, laparoscopic isthmoplasty.
